= Run report: `k = 4` exponent ladder (ecbench), 2026-10-15T04:57Z

*Descriptive.* What ran, and what it recorded. Interpretation is in the study's
`README.md` and `REPORT.pdf`.

- *Study:* `research/gaudry_quartic_d4_exponent_20261015`, protocol `PROTOCOL.md`
  (registered at `08722a2b7`; amendments 1–3). Code `0bea75038`; `ecbench`
  sha256 `8627cd29…0aa3`.
- *Specs:* `specs/SPEC-<job>.json`, one per (arm, `p`, target); generated by
  `make_specs.sh`. Queue: `jobs.txt` (amendment 1 order), run by
  `run_queue.sh`, `run_queue2.sh`, `run_queue3.sh`; log `sessions/queue.log`.
- *Host:* Claude Code cloud container, Intel Xeon @ 2.80 GHz, 4 vCPU at launch,
  3 (CPUs 0–2) from about 16:30Z; rustc 1.97.0. Every session ran with
  `--allow-busy`: isolation earned L0 (229 records) or L1 (11). `S` is a count
  (`priced_by = counted`) and does not depend on wall time; wall time below is
  descriptive only.
- *Workloads:* `fp4_torsion(p, seed 1, max_cofactor 16)`,
  `p ∈ {29, 37, 53, 61, 101, 149, 197, 293, 401, 509, 701, 1009}`; target seed
  `2026101500000 + 10p + t` (IC specs, one target each), `2026101590000 + p`
  (rho-only, 16 targets); measurement seed `202610150`.
- *Arms:* `rho-neg` (`rho.negation`); `ic-d4-w` (`ic.pipeline`,
  `fghr-y-line:zero=1`,
  `gaudry-d4:macaulay=26,weighted=1,chains=1,sparsest=1,replay=1,charge_unsolved=1`,
  `linalg=wiedemann`); `ic-d4-lp2` and `ic-d4-lp1` (the same with
  `large_primes=2` and `1`).

== Runs requested and completed

72 jobs were planned. *59 ran and completed*; every record in them verified
(`[d]G = Q`): 27 `ic-d4-w`, 9 `ic-d4-lp2`, 12 `ic-d4-lp1`, and 240 `rho-neg`
records (219 distinct; the IC specs' paired rho runs repeat the same seed when
two arms share a target). *13 did not start before the 16 h stop*
(`sessions/NOT_RUN.txt`, `NOT_RUN3.txt`): `main-p{29,37,53,61,197}-t2` and
`lp2-p{29,37,53,61,149,197,293}-t1`. 20 jobs failed at launch at about 16:28Z
("CPU n is outside this process's cpuset"; logs `sessions/*.launch-failed.log`,
no computation) and were relaunched (amendment 3); 7 of them completed, 13 are
the ones above. From 16:31Z to 20:34Z the relaunched jobs ran pinned to one CPU
(wall only).

